(PRC-06b - the removal statement is rmdir(2), not a general "remove this
 path": pointed at a regular FILE it refuses and the file keeps every
 byte. Under strace the call is rmdir(path) = -1 ENOTDIR. Also shows the
 path may be spelled as a format-string literal (LANGUAGE.md:4234-4236
 show literals). Shape of 'gen leaf process directory removal refuses a
 file', kind 422 (process batch C, 2026-10-05).
 Ran, from the repo root, on the installed vox v0.4.15:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-06b.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the file refused the removal
   the file is still there
   7
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
a text called 'the place' is "vf_scratch/process-control".
a text called keepsake is "{'the place'}/scratch_keepsake".
open a file for writing called scribe at keepsake.
Write "payload" to scribe.
Close scribe.
Delete directory "{'the place'}/scratch_keepsake".
On error print "the file refused the removal".
If keepsake is available then, print "the file is still there".
open a file for reading called reader at keepsake.
Print reader's size.
Close reader.
Delete the file keepsake.
